    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Issue:** `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file when run through the frai CLI, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked fine.\n\n**Root Cause:** In the `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`, only the positional arguments were being passed to the spawned `frai-gate` process. Since Commander.js treats `--ci` as an option (due to `.allowUnknownOption(true)`), it wasn't included in the variadic `args` array.\n\n**The Fix:** Modified the action handler to capture all arguments from `process.argv` that come after the `gate` command, ensuring flags like `--ci` are properly forwarded to the spawned process:\n\n```typescript\n.action(async (args: string[], options, command) => {\n  // ... \n  const gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\n  const allArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...allArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n  // ...\n});\n```\n\n**Verification:** Tested the fix by running `frai gate init --ci` in a fresh directory, which now correctly creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2705\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`.",
